  "result": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented voucher functionality for invoices. Here's a summary:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n**Updated `src/errors.js`**\n- Added `VOUCHER_EXISTS` error code for when trying to apply multiple vouchers\n\n**Updated `src/invoices.js`**\n\n1. **Modified `invoiceTotals()` function**:\n   - Now includes `voucher` field in the returned object (0 if no voucher)\n   - Updated total calculation: `subtotal - discount + vat - voucher` (clamped at 0)\n   - Returns structure: `{ subtotal, discount, vat, voucher, total }`\n\n2. **Added `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })` function**:\n   - Takes a fixed amount in cents off the invoice (after VAT)\n   - Only works on draft invoices (returns `NOT_DRAFT` error otherwise)\n   - Validates amount is a positive integer (returns `AMOUNT_INVALID` error)\n   - Restricts one voucher per invoice (returns `VOUCHER_EXISTS` error)\n   - Sets `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }` on the invoice\n   - Maintains immutability (doesn't mutate the original invoice)\n   - Returns `ok(newInvoice)` on success\n\n**Added 13 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Basic voucher application to draft invoices\n- Voucher inclusion in invoiceTotals\n- Correct total reduction after voucher applied\n- Amount validation (non-integer, zero, negative rejection)\n- Multiple voucher rejection\n- Issued invoice rejection\n- Total clamping when voucher exceeds invoice amount\n- Immutability verification\n- invoiceTotals with discounts and vouchers combined\n- Multi-line invoices with vouchers\n\n**Test Results**: All 184 tests pass (171 previous + 13 new voucher tests)",
